items=[
('Objective and novelty','Why this problem rather than a default classifier?','The assignment centres on inference. We quantify terminal-outcome differences, uncertainty and practical importance. The contribution beyond status-count EDA is a declared estimand and a defensible test, not a claim that lending risk has never been studied.','What is the primary estimand?','Mean issued rate among Charged Off loans minus that among Fully Paid loans.','Calling a familiar dataset itself novel.'),
('Dataset and provenance','What exactly did you analyse?',f"The local CSV contains {a['rows']:,} parsed records and {a['columns']} source columns; 33 are verified summary/footer records. Its hash is in the audit. The profile describes a smaller 314,168-row collection, so our results come from the CSV.",'Where was it originally downloaded?','The original URL, date and licence were not supplied; the filename does not prove them.','Claiming a Kaggle source without evidence.'),
('Types and schema','Why is a numeric-looking ID not a numeric feature?','Its magnitude does not represent a borrower attribute. We keep IDs for uniqueness checks, while grade is ordinal and purpose is nominal.','Why not code grade A-G as 1-7?','That imposes equal spacing if used quantitatively; our independence test uses category counts.','Confusing storage dtype with analytical meaning.'),
('Missingness','Why not fill every missing value with a mean?','Special-program fields can be structurally absent, and unconditional imputation would invent measurements and understate uncertainty. Tests use their own complete cases.','Is deletion unbiased?','Not necessarily; excluded cases may differ. Complete-case rules are transparent but do not prove missing-at-random.','Claiming that a large retained sample eliminates missingness bias.'),
('Outliers and IQR','Why not delete all outliers?','The IQR rule flags unusual values, not errors. Primary tests retain observations; cap and nonnegative-DTI sensitivities disclose their changed estimands.','What is the fence?','Q1 minus 1.5 IQR and Q3 plus 1.5 IQR, where IQR=Q3-Q1.','Choosing exclusions to improve p-values.'),
('Encoding','How is the course size requirement met?',f"The actual representation has {e['rows']:,} complete-case rows and {e['columns']} columns: {e['cells']:,} cells. It uses six numeric descriptors and one-hot categories, excluding ID, status and repayment fields.",'Does every test use that sample?','No. Each test uses its own required-variable complete cases; the matrix is for representation auditing.','Multiplying raw dimensions and calling it post-encoding size.'),
('Log transformations','Why use log1p for income?','Income is highly skewed; log(1+income) makes scale differences visible and admits zero. It is only an EDA transformation, not a declaration of Gaussianity.','Does the mean difference then mean dollars?','No. A comparison on a log scale would have a different estimand; our core tests retain original rate/DTI scales.','Interpreting a log-scale mean as an arithmetic dollar mean.'),
('Leakage','Why exclude recoveries and last-payment amounts?','They arise during or after repayment and are unavailable at origination. Including them in origination prediction could reveal the outcome.','Is grade known at application?','Not necessarily; issued grade/rate are origination descriptors. We do not make application-time prediction claims.','Treating every CSV column as a prospective predictor.'),
('EDA','What does the status plot establish?','It describes observed records and the size of the unresolved population. It motivates explicit denominator selection.','Can a boxplot prove a significant difference?','No; it depicts distributions. Tests and intervals quantify the specified mean contrast under assumptions.','Inferring p-values from appearance.'),
('Hypotheses','Why must H0 carry equality?','The reference distribution is evaluated at the equality null here: zero mean/proportion difference, or independence. H1 represents the research alternative.','When were hypotheses fixed?','After a small schema sample and the preliminary profile, before computing full-data group comparisons; this is not independent preregistration.','Claiming hypotheses were chosen before any exposure to the dataset.'),
('Direction','Why two-sided comparisons?','The scientific questions ask whether differences exist without selecting a sign after observing results.','Why is chi-square upper-tailed?','Squaring departures makes large values evidence against independence in any direction; it does not imply one grade direction.','Switching to one-sided after seeing a favourable sign.'),
('z and t tests','Why a t reference for means with a huge sample?','Population variances are unknown. Welch uses estimated spreads and Satterthwaite degrees of freedom; it approaches normal behaviour at large df without needing known sigma.','Does the CLT cure confounding?','No. It concerns sampling distributions, not selection, confounding or dependence.','Using large n as a universal validity argument.'),
('Welch versus pooled','What if group variances differ?','Welch directly allows unequal variances and unequal group sizes. Pooled t assumes equal population variances.','Why not first test variances and switch methods?','A preselected Welch procedure avoids a data-dependent selection rule and does not need that extra assumption.','Treating a nonsignificant variance test as proof of equality.'),
('Two proportions','What are the two term denominators?','Terminal loans in the 60-month and 36-month groups. Charged Off is the event; Current is excluded, not counted as no event.','Why pooled SE for z but not the CI?','The test imposes equal proportions under H0; the interval estimates the unconstrained difference using separate group proportions.','Using all originated loans as denominator while excluding unresolved events.'),
('Chi-square','Why six degrees of freedom for grade?','Seven grade rows and two outcome columns give (7-1)*(2-1)=6, with margins constraining independent cell variation.','Why inspect expected counts?','The chi-square reference is an approximation that can be poor in sparse cells. We verify the actual minimum expected count.','Applying a count-table test to arbitrary continuous measurements.'),
('P-values','What does an extremely small p-value mean?','Under H0 and the working sampling assumptions, a statistic at least this extreme is very unlikely. It does not measure the probability H0 is true.','Why report a bound instead of zero?','The numerical survival function underflows; mathematical tail probability is not zero.','Saying p is the chance results happened by random chance without conditioning on a null.'),
('Confidence intervals','What does 95% confidence mean?','A repeated-sampling procedure would cover the fixed parameter in 95% of comparable samples if its assumptions hold.','What is SE versus SD?','SD describes individual variation; SE describes uncertainty in an estimator. The mean-difference SE combines each variance divided by its sample size.','Assigning 95% probability to a fixed parameter after calculating the interval.'),
('Practical significance','Can a tiny p-value coexist with a negligible difference?','Yes. Large samples can detect small effects precisely. Compare effect size and the full interval with the declared practical threshold.','Where did our thresholds come from?','Transparent scale/decision examples chosen by the analyst, not verified industry standards; the grade V threshold is especially conventional.','Equating rejection with business importance.'),
('Multiple testing','Why apply Holm?','Four related hypotheses increase the chance of at least one false rejection. Holm adjusts ordered p-values to control family-wise error if individual p-values are valid.','Are the CIs simultaneous?','No. They remain marginal 95% intervals and are labelled accordingly.','Assuming Holm removes confounding or makes hypotheses independent.'),
('Assumptions and robustness','What is the weakest assumption?','Independent, representative sampling is not established. Loans can share borrowers and economic conditions, and the accepted/terminal selections are strong.','What does cap sensitivity tell us?','Whether extreme upper-tail values materially drive a mean contrast, while changing the estimand to a capped-variable mean.','Claiming robustness because p stays small alone.'),
('Alternative methods','Why not Mann-Whitney instead of Welch?','It changes the question to ranks/distributions; it is not generally a test of equal means or medians. Our primary estimand is the original-scale mean difference.','When use Fisher exact?','For sparse count tables where the asymptotic expected-cell condition fails, with an appropriate exact design.','Listing alternatives without explaining their estimands.'),
('Actual results','What are the main computed effects?',f"Rate difference is {r[0]['estimate']:.3f} percentage points; DTI difference {r[1]['estimate']:.3f}; grade Cramer's V {r[2]['estimate']:.3f}; term difference {100*r[3]['estimate']:.3f} percentage points. All declared tests reject under their working assumptions, and their intervals exceed the chosen positive thresholds.",'Does term cause these extra charge-offs?','No. The 60-month and 36-month terminal groups differ in borrower mix and maturity. The result is conditional association.','Confusing proportion units .1645 with .1645 percentage points.'),
('Limitations and causality','Why cannot this prove a causal effect?','There is no random assignment or credible causal identification design. Underwriting, borrower risk and economic vintage may affect both descriptors and outcomes.','What would improve the design?','Common-horizon cohorts, explicit censoring methods, borrower-cluster information and carefully justified adjustment or a causal design.','Adding regression and declaring causality automatically.'),
('Reproducibility','How can a reviewer reproduce the results?','Install requirements, point run_all.py at the raw CSV, generate reports, run tests/notebooks, then compile the template. The audit records the file hash and deterministic seeds.','Are notebook outputs invented?','No; their plain-Python cells were executed sequentially in fresh processes and actual stdout was saved. They inspect and cross-check results from the full-data pipeline.','Calling an unexecuted notebook validated.'),
('Professor challenges','What remains incomplete despite the calculations?','Exact original provenance and course mapping. Lecture/quiz/practice files were absent, and personal emails, contributions and code URL must be filled accurately before submission.','What if a test had failed to reject?','Report that evidence is insufficient to reject at the chosen level; discuss the CI and detectable practical range rather than claiming equality.','Hiding missing materials or inventing lecture numbers.')]
text='# Viva questions and answers\n\n25 categories, each with a main question, follow-up and common mistake. Numerical answers are drawn from this run.\n\n'
for i,(title,q,ans,follow,fa,mistake) in enumerate(items,1):
    text+=f'## {i}. {title}\n\n**Q: {q}**\n\n{ans}\n\n**Follow-up: {follow}**\n\n{fa}\n\n**Avoid:** {mistake}\n\n'
